          "source_quote": "ἀλλ’ ἐπειδὴ ὁ θεὸς δίκαιος ὢν βραβεύει τὸν ἑκάστου νοῦν, ὃ φῆς ἀληθὲς εἶναι, οὐκ ἂν ἐβουλήθη διὰ τῆς ἀριστερᾶς τοῖς δεξιοῖς τοῦτο δοθῆναι",
          "english_quote": "But since God, being just, judges each person’s mind—which you say is true—he would not have wished this to be given to those on the right through the left.",
          "issue": "The parenthetical English makes God's judging each person's mind the assertion Simon calls true. That attachment is defensible, but an important alternative is undisclosed: ὃ φῆς ἀληθὲς εἶναι can be a fronted relative expression resumed by τοῦτο, meaning the purported truth Simon offers. The subsequent reference to τὸ ὑπὸ σοῦ φερόμενον supports that alternative. These readings differ over what Simon claims to be true; the printed commas do not uniquely settle the attachment.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining both attachments and the reason for the chosen one. Compare the present wording explicitly with: 'But since God, being just, judges each person’s mind, he would not have wished what you say is true to be given to those on the right through the left.' If that alternative is adopted, review the revised English afresh. This is an interpretive disclosure issue, not a source-verification block.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
